      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — meaningful variable names, clearer structure, and a descriptive test name.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test uses descriptive variable names (`builder`, `builderWithMaxWidth`, `style`) instead of auto-generated ones, adds a Javadoc comment explaining the test's intent, and includes inline comments clarifying why the text string passed to `pad()` is the style's `toString()` representation and why both builder references point to the same object."
